    "done_when": "tests/test_dispatch_places_into_the_shared_reservation.py passes under the root .venv python. It runs in a temporary RECKON_HOME against a recording scheduler; no real sbatch, salloc, srun or scancel runs. Four cases. (1) A dispatch declaring placement, with no published reservation, reaches ensure_reservation from placement resolution in reckon/crew/dispatch.py. It holds the shared allocation, publishes it to the unkeyed record, and runs its worker as a step inside it with --overlap and the job id just published. (2) A second dispatch under a different project reads that same record, starts no allocation of its own, and runs its worker as a step in the allocation it found. Across both dispatches the recording scheduler logs exactly one allocation-obtaining request; the two step launches are not counted. (3) A backend declaring no placement is untouched: no ensure call, no request, and wrapping unchanged. (4) A legacy per-project record, the shape of placement/imas-ambix/reservation.json, is still honoured: its job id is placed into, and no hold is made. tests/test_crew_placement_reservation.py::test_an_unheld_reservation_leaves_the_declared_wrapping_unchanged is replaced by a test whose name states the ensure. The retry assertion in tests/test_ensure_holds_one_reservation.py asserts a literal attempt count that fails if _UNKNOWN_PROBE_ATTEMPTS is reduced to 1, instead of reading the module constant. The declared negative control is executed and logged. The test files importing reckon.crew.dispatch or reckon.crew.placement show 0 added failures between a base arm and a head arm, run with pytest-xdist -n 8, each arm with its own --basetemp under /tmp deleted afterwards. Stop and log df if /tmp has under 5 GB free. Every log sits under the run directory, headed with revision, tree and command and ending EXIT=. Out of scope, listed as follow_ons: adopting 1277272, and placement on the crew resume path.",
